Usage:
  go-mutesting Targets...

General options:
  --debug                       Debug log output
  --do-not-remove-tmp-folder    Do not remove the tmp folder where all
                                mutations are saved to
  --help                        Show this help message
  --verbose                     Verbose log output
  --config=                     Path to config file
  --html-output                 Generates a go-mutesting-report.html file after
                                testing is complete

File options:
  --blacklist=                  List of MD5 checksums of mutations which should
                                be ignored. Each checksum must end with a new
                                line character.
  --list-files                  List found files
  --print-ast                   Print the ASTs of all given files and exit

Mutator options:
  --disable=                    Disable mutator by their name or using * as a
                                suffix pattern (in order to check remaining
                                enabled mutators use --verbose option)
  --list-mutators               List all available mutators (including disabled)

Filter options:
  --match=                      Only functions are mutated that confirm to the
                                arguments regex

Exec options:
  --exec=                       Execute this command for every mutation (by
                                default the built-in exec command is used)
  --no-exec                     Skip the built-in exec command and just
                                generate the mutations
  --exec-timeout=               Sets a timeout for the command execution (in
                                seconds) (default: 10)

Test options:
  --test-recursive              Defines if the executer should test recursively

Arguments:
  Targets:                      Packages, directories and files even with
                                patterns (by default the current directory)
